   "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
   "body_html": "No, I didn&#39;t say the the tool is faulty necessarily. (It isn&#39;t. But you allocate memory that doesn&#39;t get freed until static objects are destroyed. And if the tool checks for leaks before then, then it will see chunks of allocated memory which have not been freed"
